@startuml
title P3 Live PTT - press, hold, release and stale-session safety
autonumber

actor User
participant "Sender Pulsar" as Sender
participant "Coordinator\nTASK-260712-3vzbbl" as Coord
participant "Receiver Pulsar" as Receiver
participant "Main program / duck controller" as Mix

User -> Sender : press and hold
Sender -> Sender : validate global key-down/up path\nor fall back to toggle
Sender -> Coord : live_start(session_id, generation,\naudience, codec, delivery=overlay)
Coord -> Receiver : live_start(...)\nsealed target set only
Coord -> Mix : pre-duck at live speech boundary

loop while hold is active
  Sender -> Coord : live_chunk(seq, chunk, capture_ts)
  Coord -> Receiver : live_chunk(seq, chunk, live policy)
  Receiver -> Receiver : bounded jitter buffer\nreject stale generation
  Receiver -> Mix : mix speech over main program

  alt receiver reconnects mid-session
    Coord -> Receiver : deny old session\nor attach only at allowed live edge
  else sender or coordinator sees backpressure
    Coord -> Sender : throttle or cancel per frozen contract
  end
end

alt release is received
  User -> Sender : release
  Sender -> Coord : live_end(session_id, generation)
else lock, quit or lost-release safeguard fires
  Sender -> Coord : live_cancel(session_id, generation, reason)
end

Coord -> Receiver : live_end or live_cancel
Receiver -> Receiver : drain bounded tail only
Coord -> Mix : release duck
Receiver -> Mix : stop stale session playback

note over Sender,Coord
TASK-260712-9wivva freezes the supported
hold-input path and fallback rules first.
end note

note over Coord,Receiver
TASK-260712-3qviqc freezes the exact message
names, chunk policy and generation semantics.
end note

@enduml
